### Page 1 of 22

```text
Planning and Development Office
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282
(Fax) 307-637-6366

MEMO
To:
Honorable Mayor Patrick Collins and Members of the City Council
From:
Charles W. Bloom, AICP, Planning and Development Director
Subject: UDC-23-00016 and UDC-23-00016-01 – County Pocket #1, Zoning
Date:
February 27, 2023

Background:
The item for consideration is a Zone Change. This is approved by ordinance.   This zoning map
amendment is City-initiated in conjunction with a City-initiated annexation.   City zoning districts are
established in conjunction with annexation.

The proposed Governing Body review schedule is as follows:
•
Introduction and referral February 27, 2023
•
Public Services Committee: March 7, 2023
•
Second Reading: March 13, 2023
•
Public Services Committee: March 21, 2023
•
Third and Final Reading: March 27, 2021

Staff evaluated the development pattern of the area, sought input from landowners, and utilized
PlanCheyenne’s Future Land Use Plan to determine appropriate zoning districts for the area.
Representatives of four of the five properties contacted staff seeking specific zones. Requested zones
were CB Community Business, MUB Mixed Use Business, and LI Light Industrial.  The CB and MUB
District requests are included in the ordinance since they comply with the Future Land Use Plan and are
compatible with the neighborhood. The LI zoning request has not been incorporated due to its proximity
to residences, a school, and not being in accordance with PlanCheyenne.

The Planning Commission considered establishment of CB Community Business and MUB Mixed Use
Business at their February 6 and 27, 2023, meetings and have recommended the Governing Body
approve that zoning for the area.  The items were heard on different dates because a property owner
requested MUB instead of the CB zone presented at the initial public hearing.  The February 6, 2023, and
February 27, 2023, staff reports are both attached.

The Planning Commission recommendation is to approve the establishment of CB and MUB zoning as
reflected in the staff reports and ordinance.

Attachments:
1. Ordinance
2. Zone Change Map (County MU to MUB and CB)
3. February 6, 2023, Planning Commission Staff Report and attachments
4. February 27, 2023, Planning Commission Staff Report and attachments

  Planning and Development Department
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Suite 202, Cheyenne WY 82001
(Phone) 307-637-6282 (Fax) 307-637-6366
```

### Page 2 of 22

```text
ORDINANCE NO. ________

ENTITLED: “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING THE OFFICIAL ZONING MAP OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE CHANGING THE ZONING CLASSIFICATION
FROM COUNTY MU MIXED USE TO MUB MIXED-USE BUSINESS
EMPHASIS AND CB COMMUNITY BUSINESS FOR TRACTS OF LAND
SITUATED IN PORTIONS OF SUNNY SIDE ADDITION AND
SUNNYSIDE ADDITION SECOND FILING, SECTION 12, T. 13 N., R. 67
W., 6TH P.M., LARAMIE COUNTY, WYOMING, GENERALLY
LOCATED EAST OF RIDGE RD. BETWEEN CHARLES ST. AND
PERSHING BLVD., WEST OF WILLS RD. BETWEEN CHEYENNE ST.
AND PERSHING BLVD., AND NORTHEAST OF THE INTERSECTION
OF PERSHING BLVD. AND WILLS RD.”

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That City staff has petitioned Governing Body for a zoning map amendment
(“zone change”) for said property in accordance with Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendment, of
the Cheyenne Unified Development Code (“UDC”) in accordance with their 2022 goal to annex
County pockets.

Section 2.  That on February 6, 2023, and February 21, 2023, the City of Cheyenne
Planning Commission conducted public hearings, reviewed the proposed zone changes that are the
subject of this ordinance, and recommended approval of said zone changes.

Section 3.  That the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne finds that the zone change
that is the subject of this ordinance meets the criteria specified in Section 2.2.1.d of the UDC.

Section 4.  That, in accordance with Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendment, Section 5.1.2,
Zoning Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the UDC, the
aforementioned application is hereby approved and the zoning classification of the real property
described as:

All of tracts 3, 4, Sunny Side Addition is hereby changed to MUB Mixed-use Business
Emphasis and All of tracts 13, 16, Sunny Side Addition and portions tracts 17 and 18,
Sunnyside Addition, Second Filing be more particularly described as follows: beginning at
the southwest corner of said tract 17; thence N. 01°01' 50' W. along the west line of said
tract 17 and the east line of Wills Road a distance of 196.64 feet to a point; thence S.
85°31'04" E. a distance of 131.68 feet to a point; thence S. 00°01'47" E. a distance of 46.81
feet to a point; thence S. 89°45'00" E. a distance of 168.73 feet to a point; thence S.
01°01'47" E. 140.11 feet to a point on the north line of Pershing Boulevard; thence N.
89°45'00" W. along the said north line a distance of 300.00 feet to the point of beginning
is hereby changed to CB Community Business.
6:47 pm, Feb 21 2023
```

